---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Description
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- SpaceFibre node that compresses and encrypts images: an OpenFibre port with four lanes and its AMD Versal GTY adapter
-- carries RMAP on virtual channel 0 (an OpenRMAP target through an N-Char adapter) and Space Packets on virtual channel
-- 1 (OpenSPP). Four channels take the samples of multispectral images of 64 x 64 samples in 48 bands of 16 bits from
-- received Space Packets, the last Space Packet of an image marked by the CPTP User Application value 1; a FIFO of two
-- Space Packets per channel takes them from the shared receive buffer of OpenSPP, so that the four compressors run in
-- parallel; every OpenCompact channel compresses the image (CCSDS 123.0-B-2) with its own configuration, the OpenCrypto
-- framer cuts the compressed image into chunks, the AES-GCM core encrypts every chunk, and OpenSPP sends every
-- encrypted chunk back as a Space Packet with the APID of its channel. The status registers of every compression
-- channel count its images, aborted images, faulty and discarded SDUs and memory errors; an ECC monitor reports the
-- corrected and detected errors of the memories of the framers, the compressors and the FIFOs.

